  "notes": ["All receivers are bound in the normal body queue and both original lists remain open. Only kind-2 geometry is compared numerically.","The source transforms the local center and local center plus/minus extent. Actor +0xC0 separately scales the core radius. Previous center and previous endpoints belong to the earlier callback, not a second set of source descriptors.","Nondegenerate initializer +0x7C is a linear local extent length times actor scale plus core radius. Ordinary updates add center travel and store the square of the sum, including when the center did not move.","A zero-extent source capsule still publishes, with identical endpoints and zero stored radii in these inlets. Reference comparisons for nondegenerate bounds allow up to three binary32 steps; per-Borg digests pin original observed bits.","Declared matrices only. Special swept attack flags, the consumer meaning of broad-field units, actual pair acceptance, animation, hardware and native gameplay are not qualified."],
